1
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:15,517
I bet you're oh so happy, Yisho.

2
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,776
You've been pushing for this forever.

3
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:19,500
Well, you got your wish.

4
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:22,080
The Seven Warlords have been abolished.

5
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:24,379
You know I stood firmly against it.

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,117
But when the guys at the top make
the call, there's no reversing it.

7
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:31,237
They should know that justice
comes with a price tag.

8
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:33,217
Who do you think is paying that price?

9
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,500
Take a step back.

10
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,070
The pity.

11
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,237
Still can't see the
bigger picture, can you?

12
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:42,057
It's because you've never
been one of the innocent

13
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,081
folks this cruel world has
chewed up and spit out.

14
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,381
Happens every day to good people.

15
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:50,390
Hurry up!

16
00:00:50,473 --> 00:00:51,303
We don't have time!

17
00:00:51,386 --> 00:00:52,216
Keep moving!

18
00:00:52,299 --> 00:00:53,140
Go, go, go!

19
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:08,837
The seven warlords are now no more.

20
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:11,157
Things are gonna get a bit rocky,

21
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:14,417
so we'll need to put our trust
in our special science group.

22
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:21,137
The power balance in this world is about
to be turned completely upside down.

23
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:25,857
That's not the only thing
upside down right now.

24
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:31,497
Word has it that Kaido and Big
Mom are joining forces in Wano.

25
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:36,937
That can't be the legendary

26
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:38,740
Rocks Pirates have returned!

27
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:48,440
Nothing legendary about this mess.

28
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,052
It's as real as it gets.

29
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:52,220
And it's our problem to deal with.

30
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:56,457
Unfortunately, they don't
care how busy we are.

31
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:59,128
They're just the latest
fiasco on our plate.

32
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:03,680
Two Emperors of the Sea teamed up?

33
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:06,357
There's no way.

34
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:08,657
They're really pulling this right now?

35
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:12,799
Well, technically speaking, the
intel reports they're about to unite.

36
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:15,957
There's been no damages as of this moment,

37
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:19,037
but we don't understand their
motives or how to handle this yet.

38
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:22,800
We only have a single detail
confirmed at this current time.

39
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:26,024
They both hail from the
notorious rocks pirates.

40
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:30,592
Though actual details on the
rocks crew are fairly sparse.

41
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:35,587
Big Mom and Kaido have been at
odds with one another for ages.

42
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:37,977
So this is coming out of left field.

43
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:40,217
Can't say I could have predicted this one.

44
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:42,920
If I may, who are the Rocks Pirates?

45
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:44,360
Ah, of course.

46
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:49,035
You wouldn't know much about them
since they came long before your time.

47
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:53,057
The Rocks Pirates were a
gang of extremely dangerous

48
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:56,846
individuals who came together on
the pirate island of Fullalad.

49
00:02:57,040 --> 00:03:01,880
Their entire allegiance was founded
in order to make one big score.

50
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:08,637
They were such a vicious
bunch of scoundrels

51
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:11,249
that they'd often kill
their own crewmates.

52
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:17,800
Captain Rock's lineup consisted
of many heavy hitters.

53
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:21,860
This included Whitebeard,

54
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:25,920
Big Mom.

55
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,980
and Kaido.

56
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:36,440
I know that it's hard to
believe, but trust me,

57
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:39,564
they were all once part
of the same pirate crew.

58
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:43,330
What?!

59
00:03:43,413 --> 00:03:44,243
That's crazy!

60
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:46,281
I can hardly believe that's true!

61
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:47,657
Amazingly enough,

62
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:52,217
those three weren't the only crew members
who went on to make a name for themselves.

63
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,580
Just as an example,

64
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:57,878
some of the other prestigious members
included Chaka the Golden Lion,

65
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:02,580
The Silver Axe, Captain
John and Wong Ji. Seriously?

66
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:06,497
All those maniacs were on the same crew
and they didn't wipe each other out?

67
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,051
But how can this story be lost to history?

68
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:11,560
If they hated their crewmates that much,

69
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:14,448
well, they wouldn't
want to tell their tale.

70
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:20,060
Back then, Captain Rocks was
fighting to be king of the world.

71
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:31,977
They were openly hostile
to the government.

72
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:34,617
They should have been
considered terrorists.

73
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:37,237
But many of their incidents
were covered up because

74
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:40,261
the truth was discomforting
and made us look weak.

75
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:42,260
Not that it mattered,

76
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:47,167
but when they ruled the seas, everyone
was well aware of the threat they posed.

77
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,132
Then the news broke out.

78
00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:50,617
The God Valley incident.

79
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:52,320
Just 38 years ago.

80
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,351
According to the reports,

81
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:57,297
the fiercest crew in the world,

82
00:04:57,380 --> 00:05:01,280
the Rocks Pirates, had been
completely annihilated on that island.

83
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:40,037
That rampaging force of evil
that no one was able to stop

84
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:44,120
before had been crushed by
the Navy Vice Admiral Garp.

85
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:49,268
His name soon reached
the ends of the world.

86
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:52,975
That day he became known as
the Great Hero of the Navy.

87
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:59,385
I knew he was a badass, but I
never heard how he got that title.

88
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:01,051
He's more than earned it.

89
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:07,847
I've heard a hundred tales of
heroism about Vice Admiral Garp.

90
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:11,372
It's hard to believe such an
important one when unnoticed.

91
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:15,480
He's really taken on all the
big-shot pirates, and he won no less.

92
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:22,520
Big Mom and Kaido have
allied with each other?

93
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,400
When can we catch a break?

94
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:31,317
You haven't heard much because the
man himself refuses to talk about it.

95
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,230
Why's that?

96
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:37,797
Even if he doesn't like it much, I'll tell
you the tale so it isn't lost to history.

97
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:41,697
There were two reasons why this
was never reported to the presses.

98
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:46,251
The first being he had to work alongside
pirates in order to win the battle.

99
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:48,620
Are you joking?

100
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:50,474
That's not everything.

101
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:53,425
He protected the Celestial
Dragons in doing so.

102
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:55,460
Hang on a moment.

103
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:57,660
How did they tie into all of this?

104
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:02,760
So what?

105
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:05,977
Isn't it the Navy's duty
to keep them safe, though?

106
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,400
I don't see a problem.

107
00:07:08,460 --> 00:07:11,477
It's Garp's own moral compass
that tells him otherwise.

108
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:16,097
A major reason why he's refused the
promotion to Admiral stems from the

109
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:20,477
fact that it would place him directly
under the Celestial Dragon's command.

110
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:22,897
It's his accomplishments
and reputation that

111
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:26,098
prevent him from being
dismissed for insubordination.

112
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,661
Brace yourself for the next part.

113
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:30,817
Garp had to act quickly to protect the

114
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:33,757
Celestial Dragons and
their slaves at God Valley.

115
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:37,057
With no other options left,
he joined forces with Roger.

116
00:07:37,140 --> 00:07:40,964
Together, they pooled their numbers
to defeat the Rock's pirates.

117
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:43,787
That is the truth of
the God Valley incident.

118
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,520
Like Gold Roger?

119
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:49,916
King of the Pirates?

120
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,270
They fought together?

121
00:07:51,353 --> 00:07:54,597
Celestial Dragons, Gold
Roger, and the Rocks Pirates?

122
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,660
You listed off so many big names.

123
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:59,757
Hard to believe all those people
were there at the same time.

124
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:02,840
How have I not even heard
of this God Valley place?

125
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,060
It's no surprise there.

126
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:09,140
Look for it on a modern day map.

127
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:13,380
You won't find that
island's name anywhere.

128
00:08:16,060 --> 00:08:17,740
For good reason, too.

129
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:20,800
It disappeared without a trace.

130
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:27,897
The government wanted to hide
what happened on that island,

131
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,568
and they made it disappear.

132
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:33,672
Knowing this, do you still
want to hear more of the story?

133
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:37,217
In the end, Rox was thwarted
by his own ambition.

134
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:39,500
He broke one too many taboos.

135
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:42,597
The tales of his heinous crimes
were deemed unfit for the public,

136
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:45,380
and so he came to exist only in legend.

137
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,677
It is a legacy that only lingers in the

138
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:51,740
memories of a few old
marines from my generation.

139
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,800
It's hard to imagine it.

140
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:55,497
I know this was years ago,

141
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:59,117
but it's crazy to think one man
led three of the four emperors.

142
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:02,017
Captain Rocks was Gold
Roger's very first enemy,

143
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,280
and perhaps his greatest one as well.

144
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:09,528
That aside, there was something very
interesting that those two had in common.

145
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:14,440
Though it was rarely spoken, Rock's
full name was Rocks D. Jibak.

146
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:18,860
He had a special trait some pirates
share, that being the D initial,

147
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,966
although he is no longer
alive to speak of it.

148
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:42,671
It's true that Kaido and Big Mom were
once shipmates under the same captain.

149
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:48,740
However, that was 38 years ago, and they
were nothing like they are at the present.

150
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:51,436
If the intel we received is accurate,

151
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:55,477
then this would be the birth of the
most dangerous pirate crew in the world.

152
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:59,137
All right, Brain, why don't you tell
us what everyone's bounties will be?

153
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,360
With pleasure,

154
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:02,297
but keep in mind that
we'll have to go back to

155
00:10:02,380 --> 00:10:04,517
the drawing board on the
bounties for the Warlords,

156
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,877
since they've had their
immunity stripped away.

157
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:10,725
As for the other big shots, we
can go over their numbers easily.

158
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:23,097
Let's start with the
newest Emperor of the Sea,

159
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:25,277
who attained his title about a year ago.

160
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,420
I'm sure you know.

161
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:30,857
He gained popularity after
his assault on Impel Down

162
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:34,417
two years back Now occupying
the pirate island Fuller

163
